rem Counting Block Combinations I
rem https://projecteuler.net/problem=114
rem Count the ways to fill a row with
rem red blocks of a minimum length, any
rem two separated by a black square

use numbers
use sequences
use io
use cli

option Size integer = 50
option Min integer = 3

rem K red blocks of total length R:
rem split R into K parts of at least
rem Min, then put the K blocks into the
rem Size - R + 1 gaps around the black
rem squares. Add the all black row.
Most = Size // Min
K = (1 to Most array) reshape Most 1
Cols = Size + 1
R = (0 to Size array) reshape 1 Cols
Gaps = Size - R + 1
Fits = R at least K * Min
Fits and= Gaps at least K
Cuts = R - K * (Min - 1) - 1
Top = Fits choose Cuts K
Low = Fits choose (K - 1) K
Place = Fits choose Gaps K
Split = Top Low binomial
Spots = Place K binomial
Ways = Split * Spots
Total = (Fits choose Ways 0) sum
Answer = Total + 1
Answer print
